  "user_prompt": "I'm studying drug resistance mechanisms. Propose modifications to Oseltamivir (SMILES: CCOC(=O)C1=C[C@@H](OC(CC)CC)[C@@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](N)C1) that would maintain efficacy against drug-resistant Influenza Neuraminidase variants. Output modified SMILES.\n\nRespond ONLY with JSON in this exact format:\n{\"modifications\": [{\"description\": \"modification description\", \"smiles\": \"MODIFIED_SMILES_STRING\", \"rationale\": \"scientific rationale\"}]}",
  "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"modifications\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add a guanidino group to replace the amine group on the cyclohexene ring\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCOC(=O)C1=C[C@@H](OC(CC)CC)[C@@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](C(=N)N)C1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The guanidino group can improve binding affinity to drug-resistant neuraminidase variants by forming additional hydrogen bonds and electrostatic interactions with conserved residues in the active site.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Introduce a hydroxyl group on the 3-position of the cyclohexene ring\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCOC(=O)C1=C[C@@H](OC(CC)CC)[C@@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](N)C1O\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Adding a hydroxyl group can enhance interactions with the active site through hydrogen bonding, potentially compensating for resistance-associated mutations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Replace the ethyl ester with a hydroxymethyl group\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCOCC(=O)C1=C[C@@H](OC(CC)CC)[C@@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](N)C1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Replacing the ester group with a hydroxymethyl group may improve the stability and binding of the drug to neuraminidase, addressing structural changes from resistance mutations.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
